{
 "source": "Myrow, P. M., Pope, M. C., Goodge, J. W., Fischer, W., and Palmer, A. R., 2002. Depositional history of pre-Devonian strata and timing of Ross orogenic tectonism in the central Transantarctic Mountains, Antarctica. GSA Bulletin 114, 1070–1088, fig. 1.",
 "method": "Traced by eye from the figure and placed with its graticule (scripts/outcrops_myrow2002.py); simplified to a few km. Present-day outcrop, not depositional extent. Granite intrusions inside the upper Byrd Group areas are not cut out.",
 "stratigraphy_note": {
  "ko": "Myrow et al. 2002의 개정 층서: 섀클턴 석회암 위를 얇은 홀리오크층이 덮고 그 위에 스타샷층이 쌓인다. 더글러스층(역암)은 홀리오크층 높이부터 스타샷층과 옆으로 맞물리는 안쪽(대륙 쪽) 쐐기다. 지질도는 셋을 상부 버드층군으로 묶는다.",
  "en": "Myrow et al. 2002, revised stratigraphy: the thin Holyoake Formation caps the Shackleton Limestone and the Starshot Formation lies above; the Douglas Formation (conglomerate) is an inboard wedge interfingering with the Starshot from the Holyoake level up. The map groups the three as the upper Byrd Group."
